icense":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["gradual-typing","python","static-typing","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":280,"open_issues":191,"watchers":1713,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"I just presented on this topic for PyCon Belarus, and again at WarGaming, located here in Minsk.  One question raised (and emailed to me) at the second presentation was this example.  What would be the best approach to coding this to pass the type checker (and do we need the PEP to address a similar example)? This pattern of guarding a return value seems commonplace, and avoiding superfluous warnings is desirable.\n\n% cat sergey_example.py\n\n``` python\nfrom typing import Union, Any\nfrom random import random\n\ndef db_get(key: str) -> Union[str, None]:\n    if random() < .5:\n        return \"string\"\n    else:\n        return None\n\ndef handle_result(res: str) -> Any:\n    pass\n\nresult = db_get(\"my_key\")\nif result is None:\n    pass\nelse:\n    handle_result(result)  # ???\n```\n\n% mypy sergey_example.py\nsergey_example.py, line 17: Argument 1 to \"handle_result\" has incompatible type \"Union[str, None]\"; expected \"str\"\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/typing/issues/56/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/typing/issues/56/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":232176176,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjMyMTc2MTc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/232176176","actor":{"login":"JukkaL","id":1107911,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDc5MTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11